findings.recommendation:
Strip the categories that carry no legitimate meaning in a 40-character group label before trimming, and re-check emptiness afterwards:

```ts
// eslint-disable-next-line no-control-regex
const UNSAFE_TITLE_CHARS = /[\u0000-\u001F\u007F-\u009F\u200B-\u200F\u202A-\u202E\u2066-\u2069\uFEFF]/g;

export function sanitizeGroupTitle(value: unknown): string {
  if (typeof value !== 'string') return '';
  return value.replace(UNSAFE_TITLE_CHARS, '').trim().slice(0, GROUP_TITLE_MAX_LENGTH);
}
```

Add unit cases: `sanitizeGroupTitle('\u200B')` -> `''`, `sanitizeGroupTitle('a\nb')` -> `'ab'`, `sanitizeGroupTitle('\u202Eexcatf')` -> `'excatf'`. Note this also makes the Decision 7 promise ("whitespace-only equals empty") true for the invisible-character case, and it belongs here rather than in Task 8 because the input field's `maxlength` cannot filter characters.

Either tighten the comment to say the *sanitizers* never throw while the loop still assumes a board-shaped board, or make the loop match the promise — three cheap guards that stay clear of the out-of-scope `result.boards` question:

```ts
for (const board of result.boards) {
  if (!board || typeof board !== 'object') continue;
  board.groupOrder = sanitizeGroupOrder(board.groupOrder);
  const groups = board.groups;
  if (!groups || typeof groups !== 'object') continue;
  for (const group of Object.values(groups)) {
    if (!group || typeof group !== 'object') continue;
    group.title = sanitizeGroupTitle(group.title);
  }
}
```

If the guards are added, note in the decisions log that they do not make such files loadable on their own — cleanup.ts still throws on them.
